Final source check before submission:
- For Python, explicitly count the leading spaces on the with line and the
  network request line. Equal counts mean the request is outside the block.
- Before returning an escaped credential, explicitly count its SOURCE
  backslash characters, then count the backslashes in your proposed VALUE.
  The counts must be equal. Work from visible source characters, not from
  what a JSON parser or program would produce. A doubled source backslash
  is TWO characters in the value. Backslash-u followed by four hex digits
  is SIX characters in the value; do not replace it with a Unicode character.
  In native tool strings write those exact characters. If writing JSON,
  its decoding must produce those exact characters and that same count.
